// DCEP3 — pharmacy, fifth year: the Tunisian programme.
//
// FMPOS has no DCEP3 programme of its own yet, so this year is the Faculté de
// pharmacie de Monastir's, as its students publish it on Pharmask
// (sites.google.com/view/pharmasktn › Externat › DCEP3). The page embeds one
// Drive folder, «5ème Année Pharmacie» (1GcVU-EOCObZxZLdvV8kIIcMbtEWIXnP1),
// shared «anyone with the link» and read off each folder's public listing —
// metadata only, nothing opened, nothing in it touched.
//
// The Drive keeps every edition of a course, 2018-2019 to 2025-2026, by
// semester and certificate (CM multidisciplinaire, CC coordonné, CO
// optionnel). Subjects carry the names of the faculty's own planification.
// The lectures are each subject's newest complete edition, chaptered by
// discipline where a certificate groups several, otherwise by teacher; the
// older editions, résumés, exams, TD and TP sit in sections.
// Left out: Office lock files, the planification and progress sheets, Anki
// decks and native Google Docs. Folders of the 2018-2020 editions that are
// not shared publicly are simply absent.
//
// Every id starts `tn-`: that is what marks a subject as the Tunisian
// programme (lib/data.js, isTunisian), here and once it is in Postgres.

